Chapter: DeskWelcomeBoxTest
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 WORKS-52. The welcome frame is the one surface that places itself rather
 than being laid out, and its vertical placement never learned that the task
 band docks to any edge. `dk-win-x` went through `dk-cbox-x` when the band
 became dockable and `dk-win-y` did not, so one axis is edge-aware and the
 other subtracts a bottom band unconditionally.

 THE ASSERTION IS AGAINST THE CONTRACT, NOT AGAINST THE SAME ARITHMETIC
 (L-BOTHARMS). The rect comes from `dk-win-x`, `dk-win-y`, `dk-win-w` and
 `dk-win-h`; the box comes from the four `dk-cbox-*` functions every window
 rectangle already reads. Containment is what the two roads must agree on. A
 row comparing either against itself would pass under any edge.

 ALL FOUR EDGES ARE REQUIRED. At the bottom the two roads agree by
 construction, which is the default and is why nothing has seen this; the
 rows that can fail are top, left and right. The band is SET and re-measured
 per row, because `dk-task-px` falls back to the height floor when the cell is
 unwritten and an arm that only ever ran at the default would be reporting the
 fallback rather than the layout.

 The face is `gfont-none`: `gfont-load` needs a volume and the battery
 attaches none, so this is the faceless path the sibling arms use for the same
 reason (L-NAMED). `codex/test/apps/desk-welcome-scale` is where the face half
 of this frame's arithmetic is measured.

Section: Body

  dwb-yn : Boolean -> Text
  dwb-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "NO"

 CONTAINMENT IS THE WEAKER HALF AND ON ITS OWN IT EXONERATES THE RIGHT EDGE.
 The frame is 720 device pixels in a 1280 box, so centring it in the wrong
 span moves it without moving it OUT of anything, and every containment row
 still answers yes. Centres are compared doubled, so the halving that both
 placements do is not the thing being checked, and within one pixel because
 an odd span loses a half to integer division.

 THE TWO AXES ARE REPORTED SEPARATELY because they fail for different reasons
 and a combined verdict hides one behind the other: the left-edge row is
 correct horizontally and wrong vertically, and reading one "NO" would credit
 the whole row to the vertical defect.

  dwb-near : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  dwb-near (a) (b) = if a >= b then a - b <= 1 else b - a <= 1

  dwb-row : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  dwb-row (w) (h) (ds) (e) =
    let sp = poke-32 ds dk-task-edge-cell e
    in let tk = dk-task-init ds gfont-none w
    in let s = dk-win-s w h gfont-none ds
    in let rx = dk-win-x w s ds
    in let ry = dk-win-y w h s gfont-none ds
    in let rr = rx + dk-win-w * s
    in let rb = ry + dk-win-h gfont-none s * s
    in let bx = dk-cbox-x w ds
    in let by = dk-cbox-y w ds
    in let br = bx + dk-cbox-w w ds
    in let bb = by + dk-cbox-h w h ds
    in "edge " & dk-edge-name e
       & "  " & integer-to-text w & "x" & integer-to-text h
       & "  frame " & integer-to-text rx & "," & integer-to-text ry
       & " to " & integer-to-text rr & "," & integer-to-text rb
       & "  box " & integer-to-text bx & "," & integer-to-text by
       & " to " & integer-to-text br & "," & integer-to-text bb
       & "  inside " & dwb-yn (rx >= bx & ry >= by & rr <= br & rb <= bb)
       & "  centred-x " & dwb-yn (dwb-near (rx + rr) (bx + br))
       & "  centred-y " & dwb-yn (dwb-near (ry + rb) (by + bb))

  dwb-sweep : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  dwb-sweep (w) (h) (ds) = act
    print-line-uni (dwb-row w h ds dk-edge-bottom)
    print-line-uni (dwb-row w h ds dk-edge-top)
    print-line-uni (dwb-row w h ds dk-edge-left)
    print-line-uni (dwb-row w h ds dk-edge-right)
  end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in act
      dwb-sweep 1280 800 ds
      dwb-sweep 1600 900 ds
    end

